<title>UK: Arjo Wiggins Q1 turnover down 15 pct.</title>
<headline>Arjo Wiggins Q1 turnover down 15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-French paper and packaging group Arjo Wiggins Appleton Plc said on Friday that turnover for the three months to March 31, 1997 had fallen 15.2 percent to 816 million stg.  </p>
<p>It said in a statement that at constant exchange rates the decrease was 4.4 percent.</p>
<p>The company said volumes were 5.5 percent higher but that average prices at constant exchange rates were down 9.5 percent, reflecting the lower cost of pulp.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
